Base/geometry/\nxml/json/project/raster and developer CLI members are scaffolding for ports.\nDomain crates forbid unsafe; native FFI belongs to a later audited platform crate.\nNo external dependency adoption. Shared Span(start,end) uses checked arithmetic\nand slices. Point/Affine are f64 SVG geometry, compose maps right first.\nCoordinator owns manifests/lock/contracts. Build success is not product parity.\n\nExact compiler pin1.99.0 is recorded. The host stable alias resolves to it, so\nchecks use +stable after exact-version verification without global installs.\nBuild/cache/tmp output repo-local. Six disjoint foundation owners port modules\nbehind these interfaces, with focused checks and original fixture preservation.\n# ADR0024: Rust native system services boundary\n\nAccepted2026-10-14 for macOS13 AppleSilicon native services only. No external\ncrate or first-party C shim. Rust safe wrappers encapsulate tiny audited unsafe\nFFI module, crate deny unsafe plus allow only sys and deny unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn.\nABI types/prototypes checked against local SDK headers and primary docs; foreign\nfunctions borrow buffers/fds only synchronously. No unsupported OS implementation.\n\nServices: Apple Security SecRandomCopyBytes using documented NULL default\nprovider, bounded<=256bytes, check returned status and clear output on failure;\ngetuid and getpeereid through System with u32 uid/gid, BorrowedFd and immediate\nerrno capture. Test actual OS success and pure failure classification without\nfaking native security certification. Other platform/window/file/graphics/AX\nservices remain future scopes; AppKit dependency choices not adopted here.\n\nPrimary sources fetched2026-10-14:\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/ffi.html\n- https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/secrandomcopybytes(_:_:_:)\n- https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/ksecrandomdefault\n- https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man3/getpeereid.3.html\nApple Markdown establishes availabilitymacOS10.7 and defaultconstant=NULL;\ngetentropy localman recommends Security for clients needing random bytes.\nAPI facts only, no external algorithm/editor source copied.\n# Vexel: full Rust port and product delivery\n\n## Active repository goal\n\nPort all first-party Vexel code and in-repo tooling to Rust, preserving behavior\nand supported file formats, then deliver the complete vector-editing/cartoon\nanimation product in ADR0018: modern custom UI; Inkscape SVG interchange and\nsource preservation; native artwork/animation/assets/recovery; measured large\nfile responsiveness; live visible user-controlled Codex/Claude MCP; final\nsoftware acceptance; recorded character+animation example for website/README.\n\nOwner direction2026-10-14 supersedes C17 delivery and the old two-writer ceiling.\nLegacy C checkout and all worker candidates/evidence are preserved. No finished\nRust port or performance gain is claimed. The previous goal tracker is paused;\nits API rejected replacement while unfinished. This file is the authoritative\nreplacement repository goal; the old goal was not marked achieved.\n\n## Immediate execution\n\nSix read-only Luna codex exec research lanes: build/toolchain/tools; macOS/UI;\nowned XML/SVG/raster; document/project/animation/recovery; MCP/concurrency;\ncomplete inventory/dependency/parallel sequencing. Use subscription auth and\nStandard service; no API billing switch or credit purchase. Each worker gets a\nthin scope and bounded report, no recursive agents. After synthesis, freeze\ncrate interfaces, dependency/provenance decisions and separate Rust work orders,\nthen launch as many disjoint ready implementation lanes as resources/allowance\npermit. One writer per module; one coordinator for Cargo/lock/interface changes.\n\n## Migration gates\n\n1. Inventory every first-party code file and map ownership/behavior/test evidence.\n2. Establish macOS-only Cargo workspace, toolchain